  "rules": [
    "Two-field composition: a paper field carries the question and its chart; a deep ultramarine panel carries the evidence numbers. Scripts choose roles, never sizes, colours or coordinates.",
    "Equal outer margins (112 px on paper, 96 px inside the panel, top and bottom alike); evidence facts are spaced evenly inside the panel.",
    "Weight carries hierarchy: bold serif title, regular serif numbers and claim, medium sans for kicker and captions, regular sans for information. Minimum 19 px; shorten copy rather than shrink type.",
    "One accent quantity per chart; vermilion only for a genuine comparison or held-out check, in its light form on the panel.",
    "One central question and at most four evidence numbers (three or four use value_compact).",
    "Derived numbers in the claim must agree with the displayed, rounded numbers.",
    "Titles and prose are composed separately per language; numbers, scope and conditions agree.",
    "Exact named font faces; no synthetic weight, silent fallback or bundled font files. Review at 1920, 900 and 390 px."
  ]
